     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas it meant to be one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
